<DemoExample Title="Width" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" Id="example8" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>FitWidth</b> shrinks the navbar to the width of its own content, and <b>FullWidth</b> stretches it
        over the full width of its container. Without either one the navbar takes the width its container
        gives it. Those two size the bar; <b>Justified</b> sizes the options inside it, giving each one an
        equal share instead of the width of its own label, which is how a navigation bar keeps its
        destinations on a predictable grid.
