<DemoExample Title="Header & Footer" RazorCode="@example19RazorCode" Id="example19">
    <div>
        <b>HeaderTemplate</b> and <b>FooterTemplate</b> render content before and after the options and
        outside of the list the options form, so whatever they hold is not counted among the destinations by
        a screen reader: the logo or the menu button of a bar, and the button a navigation rail is
        conventionally headed or ended with. The options move into the <b>Options</b> element here, since the
        navbar now receives more than one piece of content.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Bar:</div><br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarOption">
            <HeaderTemplate>
                <BitImage Src="/_content/Bit.BlazorUI.Demo.Client.Core/images/bit-logo.svg" Width="32" />
            </HeaderTemplate>
            <Options>
                <BitNavBarOption Text="Home" IconName="@BitIconName.Home" />
                <BitNavBarOption Text="Products" IconName="@BitIconName.ProductVariant" />
                <BitNavBarOption Text="Academy" IconName="@BitIconName.LearningTools" />
                <BitNavBarOption Text="Profile" IconName="@BitIconName.Contact" />
            </Options>
            <FooterTemplate>
                <BitButton IconOnly Title="More" Variant="BitVariant.Text" IconName="@BitIconName.More" />
            </FooterTemplate>
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br /><br />
    <div>Rail:</div><br />
