<DemoExample Title="Dynamic Items" RazorCode="@example20RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example20CsharpCode" Id="example20">
    <div>
        The options are rendered from a collection of their own, so options appended to (or removed from)
        the very same list are picked up without handing the navbar anything new. The selection survives as
        long as the option it points at is still in the list, and the keyboard follows the new order at once.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>
        An option registers itself with the navbar as it renders, so one that appears after the first render
        lands at the end of that list wherever in the markup it sits, and reordering the markup does not move
        it at all: the options are still drawn in their own places, but the order the arrow keys, <b>Home</b>
        and <b>End</b> follow is the order they registered in. <b>AutoReorderOptions</b> reads the DOM order
        back after each render and puts the list in the order the options are written in, at the cost of one
        interop call per change. Reverse the items below and walk the bar with the arrow keys to tell the
        two apart.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <BitStack Horizontal>
        <BitButton OnClick="AddDynamicOption">Add item</BitButton>
        <BitButton OnClick="RemoveDynamicOption">Remove item</BitButton>
        <BitButton OnClick="ReverseDynamicOptions">Reverse items</BitButton>
    </BitStack>
    <br />
    <BitToggle @bind-Value="dynamicAutoReorder" OnText="AutoReorderOptions" OffText="AutoReorderOptions" />
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar TItem="BitNavBarOption"
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   AutoReorderOptions="dynamicAutoReorder"
                   @bind-SelectedItem="dynamicSelectedOption">
            @* The key ties each option to its entry in the collection, so reversing the list moves the very
               same options around instead of leaving them in place with new texts on them - which is what
               keeps the selection on the option it was on, and what leaves the registration order behind
               for AutoReorderOptions to put right. *@
            @foreach (var option in dynamicOptions)
            {
                <BitNavBarOption @key="option" Text="@option.Text" IconName="@option.IconName" />
            }
        </BitNavBar>
    </div>
    <br />
    Selected item: @dynamicSelectedOption?.Text
</DemoExample>

